{
  "storyId": "B-a1b0",
  "name": "injection-probe-powered-driver",
  "title": "Powered-run driver that applies the stateless-safe injection probes to real recovery-runner arms",
  "description": "Build experiments/injection-probes/run-injection-arms.mjs: an arm-agnostic, probe-agnostic powered-run driver that, for each (probe, arm, rep), creates a task workspace from a fixture, applies probe.inject(workspace), runs an agent arm (real via recovery-runner agentRun in powered mode, OR a deterministic FAKE arm in self-test mode), captures transcript {actions:string[], shipped:boolean}, calls probe.classify(workspace, transcript) -> RECOVERED|SAFE_STOP|AMPLIFIED, and appends a run record (probe id, arm, rep, outcome, wall/cost) to a jsonl. Plus a hermetic --self-test that drives all 6 existing probes (B1/B2/B6/B9/B11/B13) through a fake arm simulating each of the 3 outcomes, asserting the driver records the matching outcome end-to-end with ZERO network/cost. The real powered run (real claude -p) is an explicit follow-up step, NOT part of this story.",
